  ('949576544584078061', 'The Cry', 1964, 'Drama', 'Jan Schmidt, Boca Abrhámová, Dagmar Perlová', 'Ludvík Aškenazy, Jaromil Jireš', 'Eva Límanová, Josef Abrhám, Eva Kopecká, Jiří Kvapil, Jiří Jánoška, Josef Kábrt, Ivan Růžička, Helena Fingerlandová', null, 'While a woman is in the hospital preparing to deliver her child, her husband has all day to reflect upon his wife and their relationship. As he tends to his job as a television repairman, Slavek fondly remembers how he first met Ivana and the days they spent getting to know one another. Slavek also grows increasingly aware of the environment that surrounds him and questions the society his new child will be entering.', 'While a woman is in the hospital preparing to deliver her child, her husband has all day to reflect upon his wife and their relationship. As he tends to his job as a television repairman, Slavek fondly remembers how he first met Ivana and the days they spent getting to know one another. Slavek also grows increasingly aware of the environment that surrounds him and questions the society his new child will be entering.', 'https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/w500/tMgK4EuYvJM3B0BRB8y6N5xs1cq.jpg', 'tmdb:movie:115243'),
  ('1138678899370397197', 'The Cry of Jazz', 1959, 'Documentary, Music', 'Edward Bland', null, 'George Waller, Dorothea Horton, Melinda Dillon, Andrew Duncan, Leroy Inman, James Miller, Gavin McFadyan, Carl Dupree', null, 'Filmed in Chicago &amp; finished in 1959, The Cry of Jazz is filmmaker, composer and arranger Edward O. Bland''s polemical essay on the politics of music and race - a forecast of what he called "the death of jazz." A landmark moment in black film, foreseeing the civil unrest of subsequent decades, it also features the only known footage of visionary pianist Sun Ra from his beloved Chicago period. Featured are ample images of tenor saxophonist John Gilmore and the rest of Ra''s Arkestra in Windy City nightclubs, all shot in glorious black &amp; white.', 'Filmed in Chicago &amp; finished in 1959, The Cry of Jazz is filmmaker, composer and arranger Edward O. Bland''s polemical essay on the politics of music and race - a forecast of what he called "the death of jazz." A landmark moment in black film, foreseeing the civil unrest of subsequent decades, it also features the only known footage of visionary pianist Sun Ra from his beloved Chicago period. Featured are ample images of tenor saxophonist John Gilmore and the rest of Ra''s Arkestra in Windy City nightclubs, all shot in glorious black &amp; white.', 'https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/w500/w3AgKx1kQb7tWCBpmW0xUhUIMrl.jpg', 'tmdb:movie:151122'),
  ('946614219747148802', 'The Cry of the Owl', 1987, 'Drama, Romance, Thriller', 'Claude Chabrol, Jean Rabier', 'Odile Barski, Claude Chabrol', 'Christophe Malavoy, Mathilda May, Jacques Penot, Jean-Pierre Kalfon, Virginie Thévenet, Patrice Kerbrat, Victor Garrivier, Charles Millot', null, 'Robert is an architect and artist, in Vichy after separating from his Parisian wife. Robert finds it calms him to stand in the shadows of the home of Juliette and Patrick and watch her cook. She thinks he''s a prowler and confronts him, then invites him in...', 'Robert is an architect and artist, in Vichy after separating from his Parisian wife. Robert finds it calms him to stand in the shadows of the home of Juliette and Patrick and watch her cook. She thinks he''s a prowler and confronts him, then invites him in...', 'https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/w500/AlNbRGPJS8Cp5Ot3LuxTZQCzHMT.jpg', 'tmdb:movie:66135'),
  ('1052676006057411314', 'The Cry of the Owl', 2009, 'Drama, Mystery, Thriller', 'Jamie Thraves, Luc Montpellier, David Manion', 'Jamie Thraves', 'Paddy Considine, Julia Stiles, Karl Pruner, Phillip MacKenzie, Gord Rand, James Gilbert, R.D. Reid, Caroline Dhavernas', 'R', 'Fleeing New York City, a failed marriage and a fragile mental history, artist Robert Forrester moves to small-town Pennsylvania. There he becomes fascinated with the simple domesticity of a beautiful neighbor, watching her through the windows of her home --- until she invites him in for coffee. He is drawn into a relationship with the young woman whose boyfriend goes missing; Robert becomes a murder suspect, gradually sensing he is the target of a larger plot.', 'Fleeing New York City, a failed marriage and a fragile mental history, artist Robert Forrester moves to small-town Pennsylvania. There he becomes fascinated with the simple domesticity of a beautiful neighbor, watching her through the windows of her home --- until she invites him in for coffee. He is drawn into a relationship with the young woman whose boyfriend goes missing; Robert becomes a murder suspect, gradually sensing he is the target of a larger plot.', 'https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/w500/h9VizOOadBJixcbpswSqM0bb30c.jpg', 'tmdb:movie:18530'),
